                <pb facs="0304" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg188"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.13/29.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Scholle to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your October 3. I called upon the President this afternoon to discuss the Amnesty
                    Bill. He said he was pleased to receive my note giving the view of the
                    Government of the United States as it helped him to prove to the leaders of the
                    House and Senate that the bill was bad legislation. He assured me that he would
                    veto it on the ground of unconstitutionality and because of the bad effect upon
                    Cuba’s reputation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scholle</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
